The Green Deal integrates sustainability into all EU policies, ensuring a fair transition for workers, businesses, and citizens.', 'EU', 'climate', 'in_force', '2019-01-01'::date, 'European Commission', 'https://commission.europa.eu/strategy-and-policy/priorities-2019-2024/european-green-deal_en', ARRAY['sdg8', 'sdg13', 'other sustainability policy', 'sdg2', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'sdg12', 'eu', 'sdg15', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('82318132-4b7e-58cf-9c81-b431538eeaef', 'Regulation (EU) of the European Parliament and', 'Regulation (EU) 2017/1129 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the 14 June 1017 on the prospectus to be published when securities are offered to the public or admitted to trading on a regulated market, and repealing Directive 2003/71/EC', 'The aim of this Regulation is to ensure investor protection and market efficiency, while enhancing the internal market for capital.', 'The aim of this Regulation is to ensure investor protection and market efficiency, while enhancing the internal market for capital.', 'The aim of this Regulation is to ensure investor protection and market efficiency, while enhancing the internal market for capital.', 'EU', 'governance', 'in_force', '2017-01-01'::date, 'Clifford Chance', 'https://www.cliffordchance.com/content/dam/cliffordchance/briefings/2017/07/pd3-prospectus-regulation-eu-20171129-summary-chart-of-key-features.pdf', ARRAY['eu', 'mandatory', 'other sustainability policy', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('7572590a-0130-5f9a-9770-5b43687debdf', 'Directive of the European Parliament and of the', 'Directive 2014/95/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on Non-Financial and Diversity Disclosures', 'Directive 2014/95/EU, amending Directive 2013/34/EU, requires certain large public-interest entities with over 500 employees to disclose non-financial and diversity information. This initiative promotes transparency by mandating the disclosure of policies, risks, and outcomes related to environmental, social, and employee matters, human rights, anti-corruption, and bribery. Public-interest entities include listed companies, banks, and insurance firms. The directive aims to harmonize reporting across the EU, enabling investors and stakeholders to assess companies'' sustainability practices. It encourages the use of national or international frameworks for reporting and exempts SMEs from these requirements. Member States must transpose this directive into national law, ensuring effective mechanisms for compliance and enforcement.', 'Directive 2014/95/EU, amending Directive 2013/34/EU, requires certain large public-interest entities with over 500 employees to disclose non-financial and diversity information. This initiative promotes transparency by mandating the disclosure of policies, risks, and outcomes related to environmental, social, and employee matters, human rights, anti-corruption, and bribery. Public-interest entities include listed companies, banks, and insurance firms. The directive aims to harmonize reporting across the EU, enabling investors and stakeholders to assess companies'' sustainability practices. It encourages the use of national or international frameworks for reporting and exempts SMEs from these requirements. Member States must transpose this directive into national law, ensuring effective mechanisms for compliance and enforcement.', 'Directive 2014/95/EU, amending Directive 2013/34/EU, requires certain large public-interest entities with over 500 employees to disclose non-financial and diversity information. This initiative promotes transparency by mandating the disclosure of policies, risks, and outcomes related to environmental, social, and employee matters, human rights, anti-corruption, and bribery. Public-interest entities include listed companies, banks, and insurance firms. The directive aims to harmonize reporting across the EU, enabling investors and stakeholders to assess companies'' sustainability practices. It encourages the use of national or international frameworks for reporting and exempts SMEs from these requirements. Member States must transpose this directive into national law, ensuring effective mechanisms for compliance and enforcement.', 'EU', 'climate', 'in_force', '2014-01-01'::date, 'Official Journal of the European Union', 'https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/PDF/?uri=CELEX:32014L0095', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'eu']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('3684ce83-7062-5ddf-92a5-6472ec1a95f9', 'EU Policy on Gender Equality in Italy', 'The Policy on Gender Equality in Italy', 'Upon request of the FEMM committee, this note provides an overview of the existing gender-equality legislation and policies in Italy, focussing on their recent developments and achievements in the last decades. It discusses gender equality in employment, reconciliation of work and family life, presence of women in decision-making positions, recent measures to fight violence against women, and health and reproductive rights.', 'Upon request of the FEMM committee, this note provides an overview of the existing gender-equality legislation and policies in Italy, focussing on their recent developments and achievements in the last decades. It discusses gender equality in employment, reconciliation of work and family life, presence of women in decision-making positions, recent measures to fight violence against women, and health and reproductive rights.', 'Upon request of the FEMM committee, this note provides an overview of the existing gender-equality legislation and policies in Italy, focussing on their recent developments and achievements in the last decades. It discusses gender equality in employment, reconciliation of work and family life, presence of women in decision-making positions, recent measures to fight violence against women, and health and reproductive rights.', 'EU', 'social', 'in_force', '2014-01-01'::date, 'European Parliament', 'https://www.europarl.europa.eu/thinktank/en/document/IPOL-FEMM_NT(2014)493052', ARRAY['sdg8', 'sdg3', 'other sustainability policy', 'voluntary', 'sdg5', 'eu', 'voluntary_frameworks']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('f20392a9-a03e-5d09-bf2e-0e31cd1472cf', 'EU Best Environmental Management Practice in the Tourism Sector', 'Best Environmental Management Practice in the Tourism Sector', 'This document is intended to support environmental improvement efforts of all actors in the tourism sector. It can be used by all organisations and stakeholders of the sector who seek for reliable and proven information to improve their environmental performance. In case they have an environmental management system, such as EMAS, they can also use the document to develop it further, especially with respect to continuous environmental improvement measures and targets.', 'This document is intended to support environmental improvement efforts of all actors in the tourism sector. It can be used by all organisations and stakeholders of the sector who seek for reliable and proven information to improve their environmental performance. In case they have an environmental management system, such as EMAS, they can also use the document to develop it further, especially with respect to continuous environmental improvement measures and targets.', 'This document is intended to support environmental improvement efforts of all actors in the tourism sector. It can be used by all organisations and stakeholders of the sector who seek for reliable and proven information to improve their environmental performance. In case they have an environmental management system, such as EMAS, they can also use the document to develop it further, especially with respect to continuous environmental improvement measures and targets.', 'EU', 'climate', 'in_force', '2013-01-01'::date, 'European Commission, Joint Research Centre', 'https://publications.jrc.ec.europa.eu/repository/bitstream/JRC82602/tourismbemp.pdf', ARRAY['eu', 'voluntary', 'other sustainability policy', 'regulations']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
